d of throwing\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false } as any);\n    expect(await getReviewer()).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### B. Stubbed contracts — write these test-first, before implementing\n\nAGENTS.md explicitly scopes these by phase. Writing the tests now against the documented contract (docstrings + Severity Model + Synthetic Data spec) gives you a spec to implement against and an instant regression net.\n\n#### B1. `fold_name` — normalization (Phase 2)\n```python\n# Cases pulled directly from AGENTS.md's normalization + name-variant injection spec.\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"raw,expected\", [\n    (\"Acme Inc.\", \"acme\"),\n    (\"ACME INC\", \"acme\"),\n    (\"Acme, Inc.\", \"acme\"),\n    (\"Acme Pvt Ltd\", \"acme\"),\n    (\"Acme GmbH\", \"acme\"),\n    (\"  Acme   Corp  \", \"acme\"),   # internal + surrounding whitespace\n    (\"\", \"\"),                      # empty string, no crash\n    (\"Acme\", \"acme\"),              # no suffix present\n    (\"Inc.\", \"\"),                  # name IS the suffix — edge case worth deciding\n])\ndef test_fold_name(raw, expected):\n    assert fold_name(raw) == expected\n\ndef test_fold_name_is_deterministic_and_total():\n    # same input -> same output across repeated calls, required by AGENTS.md\n    assert fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\") == fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\")\n```\n\n#### B2. `normalize` — pure record → CanonicalEntity (Phase 2)\n```python\ndef test_normalize_preserves_original_name_alongside_folded_name():\n    entities = normalize([{\"Id\": \"001\", \"Name\": \"Acme Inc.\"}],\n                          entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"src-1\")\n    assert entities[0].name == \"Acme Inc.\"\n    assert entities[0].normalized_name == \"acme\"\n\ndef test_normalize_maps_parent_field_to_parent_external_id():\n    ...\n\ndef test_normalize_handles_missing_optional_fields_without_raising():\n    # a record with no ParentId, no LastModifiedDate\n    entities 