        "title": "B6. `generate` — synthetic data + ground truth (Phase 1)",
        "content": "```python\ndef test_generate_is_reproducible_for_the_same_seed(tmp_path):\n    r1 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"a\")\n    r2 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"b\")\n    assert r1 == r2  # or compare manifest.json contents byte-for-byte\n\ndef test_generate_different_seeds_produce_different_orgs(tmp_path):\n    r1 = generate(seed=1, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"a\")\n    r2 = generate(seed=2, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"b\")\n    assert r1 != r2\n\ndef test_generate_produces_at_least_one_ambiguous_entry_at_default_rates(tmp_path):\n    # AGENTS.md: \"deliberately inject cases where the correct answer is escalate\"\n    manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=500, out_dir=tmp_path)\n    assert any(m.expected_resolution == \"escalate\" for m in manifest)\n\ndef test_generate_injection_rate_of_zero_produces_no_divergence_of_that_type(tmp_path):\n    manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=200, out_dir=tmp_path,\n                         rates=InjectionRates(reparent=0.0))\n    assert not any(m.conflict_class == \"structural\" for m in manifest)\n\ndef test_generate_duplicate_injections_always_map_to_duplicate_class(tmp_path):\n    ...\n\ndef test_generate_writes_side_a_side_b_and_manifest_files(tmp_path):\n    generate(seed=42, accounts=10, out_dir=tmp_path)\n    assert (tmp_path / \"manifest.json\").exists()\n```\n\n",
