        "title": "C. Missing error-handling tests (cross-cutting)",
        "content": "\nNone of these paths currently have a test asserting failure behavior:\n\n1. **Engine never writes to `sources`/`rulesets`** (table ownership, AGENTS.md's hardest constraint) — no test enforces this. Once `db.py` has a writer, add a static/integration check:\n   ```python\n   def test_engine_db_module_never_references_sources_or_rulesets_tables():\n       import db\n       src = inspect.getsource(db)\n       assert \"sources\" not in src and \"rulesets\" not in src\n   ```\n2. **`validate()` failure must escalate, never crash the batch** — one bad conflict shouldn't kill `resolve()` for the rest (test a mixed batch).\n3. **Zod validation on route handlers** — none exist yet, but when they land, every one needs a \"malformed body → 400, not 500\" test (AGENTS.md: \"Every route handler validates its body with Zod before touching the database. No exceptions.\").\n4. **`requireReviewer` throwing on a route boundary** — verify it maps to a 401/redirect, not an unhandled exception leaking a stack trace.\n5. **Connector failures** (`salesforce.py`, `warehouse.py` — both stubs) — need tests for auth failure, rate-limit/retry, and partial-stream failure once implemented, since `extract()` is a generator that a caller may only partially consume.\n\n---\n\n",
